description:
Implement `createSelectableContext` which creates a context that supports fine-grained subscriptions. `useSelector` only causes a re-render when the selected slice of context actually changes (referential equality check).

**Example:**
```tsx
const ctx = createSelectableContext({ count: 0, name: 'Alice' });

function Counter() {
  // only re-renders when count changes
  const count = ctx.useSelector(s => s.count);
  return <span>{count}</span>;
}

function App() {
  return <ctx.Provider value={{ count: 1, name: 'Alice' }}><Counter /></ctx.Provider>;
}
```

